const e={readingNotes:[{title:{zh:"媒体在反映市场，还是影响市场？",en:"Does media reflect or influence markets?"},body:{zh:"Tetlock研究财经媒体的语气与市场活动之间的关系。问题不只是坏消息是否伴随下跌，还包括市场下跌是否反过来影响报道，以及这种关系能否与基本面信息区分。",en:"Tetlock examines how financial-media tone relates to market activity. The question includes whether pessimism precedes price changes, whether declines affect subsequent reporting, and how these relations differ from information about fundamentals."}},{title:{zh:"词典类别不是互斥标签",en:"Dictionary categories are not exclusive labels"},body:{zh:"第II节说明General Inquirer词典类别既不互斥，也不覆盖所有词；一个词可能进入多个类别。作者还调整星期几对应的类别均值，避免专栏的规律性写作差异主导因子。编辑建议：保留词典版本、计数口径与日历处理，不把各类别计数直接加成独立词数。",en:"Section II states that General Inquirer categories overlap and do not cover every word. Category means are also centered by weekday to reduce systematic writing-pattern noise. Editorial application: preserve dictionary versions, counting conventions and calendar treatment; summing category counts does not yield a count of distinct classified words."},reference:{url:"https://www.columbia.edu/~pt2238/papers/Tetlock_Media_Sentiment_JF.pdf",label:{zh:"原文第II节：词语分类与星期效应",en:"Original §II: word categories and weekday effects"}}},{title:{zh:"把文字转成可观察的度量",en:"Turning text into a measure"},body:{zh:"作者使用《华尔街日报》一个日常市场专栏，将词语分类并通过主成分方法构建悲观程度指标，再用时间序列方法观察它与收益、成交量的联系。这个度量依赖具体语料和词典，不是语言本身天然给出的分数。",en:"The study classifies words from a daily Wall Street Journal market column, uses principal components to construct a pessimism measure, and examines its temporal relations with returns and volume. The measure depends on a particular corpus and dictionary, not a universal language score."}},{title:{zh:"双向关系与短期反应",en:"Feedback and short-run responses"},body:{zh:"论文报告较高悲观程度与随后价格下行压力及回归相关，极端语气与较高成交量相关，市场下跌也会带来更多悲观报道。因此，单向写成“新闻决定股价”会丢失论文的重要部分。",en:"The paper reports downward price pressure followed by reversion after pessimistic media content, higher volume with extreme tone, and greater pessimism following low returns. Reducing this to 'news determines prices' omits important feedback in the evidence."}},{title:{zh:"先确定载荷，再计算下一年的文本指标",en:"Estimate loadings before scoring the next year"},body:{zh:"作者用t−1年的文本估计主成分载荷，再用这些载荷计算t年的每日因子，避免把未来语料信息带入当期度量。这个因子从词语类别的共同变化中提取，不以股票收益作为拟合目标。若改用全样本一次性训练，就改变了原研究的信息边界。",en:"Loadings estimated from year t−1 score daily content in year t, keeping future corpus information out of contemporaneous measurement. The factor extracts variation among word categories rather than optimizing against stock returns. Training once on the complete historical corpus would change that information boundary."},reference:{url:"https://www.columbia.edu/~pt2238/papers/Tetlock_Media_Sentiment_JF.pdf",label:{zh:"原文第II节：逐年主成分估计",en:"Original §II: annual principal-component estimation"}}},{title:{zh:"从旧报纸走向新语料",en:"Moving to a different corpus"},body:{zh:"本站建议先固定媒体范围、版本与发布时间，再去除转载并检查实体识别。原样本是1984—1999年的美国报纸专栏；中文公告、社交媒体和大模型标签都需要自己的人工核对样本，不能直接继承这篇论文的测量有效性。",en:"Fix the publisher universe, text version and release timing before deduplicating and checking entity mapping. The sample is a US newspaper column from 1984–1999. Chinese filings, social media and model-generated labels need their own validation samples."}}],readerLimits:{zh:"时间序列预测关系不自动等于因果效应；语料选择、语言、词典与发布时间都会限制迁移。",en:"Predictive temporal relations do not automatically establish causation; corpus selection, language, dictionaries and release timing constrain transfer."}};export{e as default};
